  "needs": {
    "container": true,
    "reason": "the Android build evaluates Gradle scripts, needs the Android SDK platform 35 and android/app/google-services.json, a secret that is not in the repository; the Tauri crate needs the system WebView libraries to build"
  },
  "traps": [
    "the callable function is joined only by a string: functions-python/main.py exports create_checkout_session (the Python function name is the deployed name), react-app/src/checkout.ts calls httpsCallable(functions, \"create_checkout_session\")",
    "the Tauri command is joined only by a string: #[tauri::command] save_receipt in react-app/src-tauri/src/lib.rs, invoke(\"save_receipt\", { orderId }) in checkout.ts; orderId becomes order_id by Tauri's argument renaming",
    "the collection name orders is written five times: shared/collections.ts (ORDERS), functions-python/main.py, MainActivity.kt, firestore.rules and firestore.indexes.json; the TypeScript trigger builds the path from ORDERS plus /{orderId}",
    "shared/ has no manifest: it is a source-tree unit (name null, named by its root) that two units compile and neither owns; shop-web reaches it through the @shared alias (tsconfig paths and Vite alias), shop-functions-ts through relative imports and rootDir \"..\" in functions/tsconfig.json, so both list it in depends_on",
    "functions/package.json main is lib/functions/src/index.js, the compiled output (rootDir \"..\" keeps shared/ in the output); the source entry is functions/src/index.ts",
    "the Tauri crate lives inside the npm unit's folder (react-app/src-tauri); its depends_on shop-web comes from tauri.conf.json (beforeBuildCommand npm run build, frontendDist ../dist), not from Cargo",
    "two Cloud Functions codebases in one firebase.json: ts (Node 20) and py (Python 3.12); nodejs20 and python312 are written only in firebase.json and functions/package.json engines",
    "the Firebase CLI installs Python functions from requirements.txt; this codebase declares its dependencies only in pyproject.toml",
    "Stripe appears with three packages: @stripe/stripe-js (browser), stripe on npm (TypeScript functions), stripe on PyPI (Python functions)",
    "android/app/google-services.json is absent although the google-services plugin needs it; firebase-firestore has no version: the platform firebase-bom 33.6.0 fixes it to 25.1.1 (read from the BOM on Google Maven), and the BOM itself is a constraint, not listed; the Gradle wrapper jar and gradlew scripts are absent",
    "no lockfile anywhere: npm, Cargo and uv locks are not reproducible by hand, every resolved is null",
    "no workspace joins the units: the only one is the Gradle build under android/; firebase.json deploys units but does not build them"
  ],
